  "definition": "Thermal balance is the accounting relationship between heat entering, generated within, stored by and rejected from a system. For a spacecraft, incoming terms include absorbed solar and planetary radiation and equipment dissipation; outgoing heat is mainly radiated to space. During a transient, the difference changes stored thermal energy and therefore temperature. At a stable steady state, net storage approaches zero.[^1]",
